        "pros": ["Easy to install, remote access via apps, and affordable.", "Helps deter damage and provides evidence if needed."],
        "cons": ["Ensure they are not in private spaces like bedrooms or bathrooms to respect privacy.", "Requires regular battery checks or power source."]
      },
      {
        "method": "Smart Sensors for Doors and Windows",
        "description": "Install sensors from brands like Ring or Philips Hue that alert you if doors or windows are opened unexpectedly. These are small and can be hidden behind fixtures.",
        "pros": ["Non-invasive and focus on entry points, providing real-time notifications.", "Low power consumption and easy integration with smart home apps."],
        "cons": ["May not cover all areas, so combine with other methods.", "False alarms from wind or pets could occur."]
      },
      {
        "method": "Noise Level Monitors",
        "description": "Use devices like smart plugs or apps that monitor sound levels (e.g., via a smartphone or dedicated device) to detect unusual activity without visual recording.",
        "pros": ["Discreet and doesn't involve video, focusing on disturbances like parties.", "Can be integrated with your phone for alerts."],
        "cons": ["Less effective for visual damage, and accuracy depends on placement.", "May pick up normal household noises."]
      },
      {
        "method": "Smart Locks and Access Control",
        "description": "Implement smart locks like August or Yale that track entry and exit times, allowing you to monitor access without constant surveillance.",
        "pros": ["Provides logs of who enters and when, enhancing security.", "Guests can use codes or apps, reducing the need for physical keys."],
        "cons": ["Requires guests to follow instructions, and technical issues could arise.", "Doesn't monitor internal activities."]
      },
      {
        "method": "Regular Virtual or Scheduled Checks",
        "description": "Use apps for virtual tours via integrated devices or schedule quick in-person inspections between stays, combined with guest feedback.",
        "pros": ["Non-tech-heavy option that builds rapport with guests.", "Allows for proactive maintenance without constant monitoring."],
        "cons": ["Less immediate than real-time alerts, and depends on your availability."]
      }
    ],
    "disclaimer": "Always check local laws and regulations regarding surveillance, as unauthorized monitoring can lead to legal issues. Inform guests about any monitoring devices in your listing and house rules to maintain transparency and trust. Prioritize ethical practices to protect both your property and your guests' privacy."
  }
}

